Subject: Keep the requested windowed size as the Wayland floating size

The window opens at the splash size, and setting the video mode to its windowed
size does not update floating_width and floating_height. The compositor's next
configure carries 0x0, the configure handlers fall back to the floating size,
and the window returns to 240x256 with the menu clipped.

--- a/gfx/common/wayland_common.c
+++ b/gfx/common/wayland_common.c
@@ -974,6 +974,11 @@
 
    if (!fullscreen)
    {
+      /* A configure event of 0x0 leaves the size to the client, which
+       * takes the floating size; keep it the requested size, or the window
+       * shrinks back to the splash size on the next configure. */
+      wl->floating_width       = wl->width;
+      wl->floating_height      = wl->height;
       wl->buffer_scale         = wl->pending_buffer_scale;
       wl->fractional_scale_num = wl->pending_fractional_scale_num;
       wl->buffer_width         = wl->fractional_scale ?
